A functional core keeps domain rules independent of external interfaces and process machinery. Fewer shared timelines remove ordering problems before coordination is added.

> Our core doesn’t access external interfaces or use any process machinery your component might use.

Source: [Q14](/lore/durability-bibliography#q14); [B3](/lore/durability-bibliography#b3-designing-elixir-systems-with-otp), [B13](/lore/durability-bibliography#b13-grokking-simplicity).

## Failure it prevents

Rules change with hidden time or shared state and can only be tested through live integrations.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

Keep pure rules as ordinary functions. `Context.Service` and `Layer` put [effectful dependencies](/lore/services-capture-dependencies) behind seams. Wrapping a callback in [Effect](/lore/effect-basics) does not make it pure.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Context.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Layer.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Effect.ts`.

## How to check

Run the same decision with the same explicit data. Check that it needs neither network nor process state. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Replay needs stable inputs](/lore/replay-needs-stable-inputs), [Recovery needs model tests](/lore/recovery-needs-model-tests).

Connect this to [the existing rat-stack guidance](/lore/layers-make-dependencies-explicit).

